<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-8922] Discovery message delivery guarantee can be violated</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-8922</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Under certain circumstances discovery messages may be delivered only to a part of nodes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It happens because pending messages are not resent due to data inconsistency in &lt;tt&gt;ServerImpl#PendingMessages&lt;/tt&gt; class. If &lt;tt&gt;discardId&lt;/tt&gt; or &lt;tt&gt;customDiscardId&lt;/tt&gt; point to a message, that is not present in the queue, then other messages will be skipped and won&apos;t be resent. It may happen, for example, when queue in &lt;tt&gt;PendingMessages&lt;/tt&gt; is overflown.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;PFA test, that reproduces this problem.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
