                            <comment id="16541268" author="dmekhanikov" created="Thu, 12 Jul 2018 07:45:21 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Please review my patch: &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/4349&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/4349&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;TC run: &lt;a href=&quot;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/project.html?projectId=IgniteTests24Java8&amp;amp;branch_IgniteTests24Java8=pull%2F4349%2Fhead&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/project.html?projectId=IgniteTests24Java8&amp;amp;branch_IgniteTests24Java8=pull%2F4349%2Fhead&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16545117" author="dkarachentsev" created="Mon, 16 Jul 2018 12:08:00 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=dmekhanikov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;dmekhanikov&quot;&gt;dmekhanikov&lt;/a&gt; in general it looks fine, but node is vulnerable for OOME or IllegalStateException, because pending message queue could grow unlimited now. Anyway, both cases: node hang due to lost messages or OOME are harmful, but last is less possible. I&apos;m OK with this change so far.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16546178" author="dmekhanikov" created="Tue, 17 Jul 2018 08:24:14 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=dkarachentsev&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;dkarachentsev&quot;&gt;dkarachentsev&lt;/a&gt;, losing discovery messages is much more harmful, since it may lead to the whole cluster being stuck.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On the other hand, if a node fails with OOME, then it&apos;s only a problem of one node. And in order to make it happen, discard messages should not be delivered for a really long time, which is quite unlikely.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So, I think, that nodes should either guarantee delivery of all discovery messages, that are passed to them, or die.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
